111
00:04:29,995 --> 00:04:31,615
It's going to handle rollover.

112
00:04:31,615 --> 00:04:33,340
That sounds like something
that will be able to

113
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:36,550
test to make sure it's
working properly.

114
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:40,170
If I wanted to use
this with unity,

115
00:04:40,170 --> 00:04:42,500
I could add some
test functions and

116
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:45,755
just prefix those with
names test underscore.

117
00:04:45,755 --> 00:04:48,110
That includes some assertions.

118
00:04:48,110 --> 00:04:49,820
Those assertions you
probably noticed

119
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:52,490
in other test case definitions
you've used for the class

120
00:04:52,490 --> 00:04:54,860
already there going
to be defined in

121
00:04:54,860 --> 00:04:56,840
UD assertions reference and

122
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:59,270
just are things
like test assert,

123
00:04:59,270 --> 00:05:03,020
and then check for
conditions like equal,

124
00:05:03,020 --> 00:05:04,340
less than, greater than

125
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:06,400
something about two
different values.

126
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:09,425
In this time-space diff case,

127
00:05:09,425 --> 00:05:11,180
I'm going to first

128
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:13,855
create a time spec that's
based on one second.

129
00:05:13,855 --> 00:05:16,775
Then at time spec that
is based on 1.1 second,

